# PROPOSAL. To be added to CODEOWNERS on the fork's branch, with branch
# protection requiring code owner review. These are the files that decide
# what the integrity proof means. Whatever maintains the fork day to day,
# a person approves changes to them.

# The proof: its rules for what to disregard, its corpus, its provider and
# its component driver. Removing a scenario, or adding a rule, weakens it.
/fork-proof/                  @cozybear-dev

# The upstream commit that the fork is compared with, and the later commits
# of upstream's that are applied to it first.
/fork-proof/UPSTREAM_REF      @cozybear-dev
/fork-proof/UPSTREAM_BACKPORTS @cozybear-dev

# The list of files the fork is allowed to differ from upstream in.
/fork-proof/FORK_FILES        @cozybear-dev

# The workflows that run the proof and publish images.
/.github/                     @cozybear-dev
/Dockerfile.fork              @cozybear-dev

# What the fork tells people it does differently.
/README-FORK.md               @cozybear-dev
